at\\tau$ over the five specifications of the ladder (regression, quadratic, spline, count and two-hop), or $B_2=\\tfrac12\\hat M[(1-p)^2+p^2]$, with $\\hat M$ the larger, over the two own-treatment arms, of the largest second derivative of a cubic in $f$ fitted in the arm, over the observed range of $f$ of the draw (noise level 0.5). The multiplier $\\kappa$ was frozen on the original cells before the block ran, as the smallest value of a grid from 0.25 to 64 at which the smooth mechanisms (a), (b), (c), (e), (f) are covered at least 90\\% of the time: $\\hat\\kappa=0.25$ for $B_2$, the floor of the grid, and 1 for $B_1$. At the floor the grid cannot say how much smaller a $\\kappa$ would still cover, so $B_2$ is a bound and not a calibration. On the 666 cells of the block (nine groups), $B_2$ covers 0.990 on average over cells (worst group, mechanism (e): 0.949) at a mean width of 8.4, and $B_1$ 0.963 (worst 0.882) at 3.3, against 0.70 for HC0 at a width of 0.68, in units of $\\gate$. The 1296 original cells, which were analysed after the results, give 0.981 at 11.0, 0.945 at 3.1 and 0.67. Where $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}>2$ (92 block cells) the coverage is 0.938 for $B_2$, 0.821 for $B_1$ and 0.153 for HC0. The width is smallest in that stratum (3.8 for $B_2$ against 11.6 at $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}$ 0.25--0.5), where the bias is largest (Figure~\\ref{fig:p6}). The median $\\kappa^\\star$, the smallest multiplier that covers, over the smooth mechanism--degree cells is 0.25 for $B_2$, within the expected bound of 2, which a bound at the floor meets trivially.\n+The interval is $\\hat\\tau\\pm c_\\alpha(\\kappa B/\\mathrm{SE})\\,\\mathrm{SE}_{\\rm HC0}$ at the 90\\% level, with $c_\\alpha(b)$ the $1-\\alpha$ quantile of $|N(b,1)|$, and $B$ one of two bounds on the extrapolation: $B_1$, the range of $\\hat\\tau$ over the five specifications of the ladder (regression, quadratic, spline, count and two-hop), or $B_2=\\tfrac12\\hat M[(1-p)^2+p^2]$, with $\\hat M$ the larger, over the two own-treatment arms, of the largest second derivative of a cubic in $f$ fitted in the arm, over the observed range of $f$ of the draw (noise level 0.5). The multiplier $\\kappa$ was frozen on the original cells before the block ran, as the smallest value of a grid from 0.25 to 64 at which the smooth mechanisms (a), (b), (c), (e), (f) are covered at least 90\\% of the time: $\\hat\\kappa=0.25$ for $B_2$, the floor of the grid, and 1 for $B_1$. At the floor the grid cannot say how much smaller a $\\kappa$ would still cover, so $B_2$ is a bound and not a calibration. On the 666 cells of the block (nine groups), $B_2$ covers 0.990 on average over cells (worst group, mechanism (e): 0.949) at a mean width of 8.4, and $B_1$ 0.963 (worst 0.882) at 3.3, against 0.70 for HC0 at a width of 0.68, in units of $\\gate$. The 1296 original cells, which were analysed after the results, give 0.981 at 11.0, 0.945 at 3.1 and 0.67. Where $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}>2$ (92 block cells) the coverage is 0.938 for $B_2$, 0.821 for $B_1$ and 0.153 for HC0.\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "e20cc6d3-8379-5448-8410-bae90940d51b", "at": 1795663290.6396072, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 157307, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "a355e4af51e4a52c394043d6d4dc0571", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "fc92a515-d1da-5e8a-b70d-116c97cb62d5", "at": 1795663290.6448553, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 157308, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "a355e4af51e4a52c394043d6d4dc0571", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], 